DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssttoorree functions are designed to copy small amounts of data to user-
     space.  If the user address is naturally aligned, then the operation will
     be performed atomically.  Otherwise it may fail or be performed non-atom‐
     ically, depending on the platform.

     The ssttoorree routines provide the following functionality:

     ssuubbyyttee()    Stores a byte of data to the user-space address _b_a_s_e.

     ssuuwwoorrdd()    Stores a word of data to the user-space address _b_a_s_e.

     ssuuwwoorrdd1166()  Stores 16 bits of data to the user-space address _b_a_s_e.

     ssuuwwoorrdd3322()  Stores 32 bits of data to the user-space address _b_a_s_e.

     ssuuwwoorrdd6644()  Stores 64 bits of data to the user-space address _b_a_s_e.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ssttoorree functions return 0 on success or -1 on failure.

